    <string name="tutorial_title_1">Hide your fleet</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_1">Arrange your pieces horizontally or vertically. Pieces cannot overlap. Use Randomize for a quick start, then Ready to lock your fleet.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title_2">Pick a target</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_2">Tap a cell on the target grid, then Fire. A flame means hit; an X means miss. Find every cell in a piece to destroy it. Try selecting B3 below.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title_3">Read the grid</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_3">A hit gives you a clue: try neighboring cells. In Classic games, a hit lets you fire again by default; a miss ends your turn. Turn this option off to alternate after every shot. In salvo games, select one shot per surviving piece before firing.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_title_4">Take your time</string>
    <string name="tutorial_body_4">There is no timer. Tap a cell, then press Fire. Pinch to zoom. Back saves your progress. Nearby matches pause when either player leaves; both original devices can reconnect later.</string>
